<workflow>
  <name>main-0008-upsert-batch-error-accounting</name>
  <name_sync_with_filename>Y</name_sync_with_filename>
  <description>pgvector upsert with an error hop on PostgreSQL, twelve chunks of which the database refuses three (a vector of the wrong size): one in the middle of the first commit window, one at the first position of the second and one at the end of the final partial window. Once at commit size 5: PostgreSQL's validated batch failure contract (the whole batch is lost) keeps batching on with the error hop, without a savepoint per row, and the good rows of a failed batch are run again. Once at commit size 0: one transaction, every row behind a savepoint, as before. Asserts for both that exactly the three bad chunks reach the error stream with code PGVECTORUPSERT002, that the nine good chunks are stored and reported once, and that no chunk is reported on the main output unless it is in the table. A third upsert deletes each document before its chunks: a document whose only new chunk is refused keeps its earlier chunks, and a document whose first new chunk is refused is still replaced by the others.</description>
  <extended_description/>
  <workflow_version/>
